  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find the derivative of $y=4sec\u2061x+{e}^{x}$ at $x=0.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{0}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we take the derivative of each term and then add them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(4sec\u2061x+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =4sec\u2061xtan\u2061x+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=0} & =(4sec\u2061xtan\u2061x+{e}^{x})\\,{|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =4sec\u2061(0)tan\u2061(0)+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
